    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "The Righteous Kingdom Announced"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Indeed, a king will reign righteously,",
          "and rulers will rule justly."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Each will be like a shelter from the wind,",
          "a refuge from the rain,",
          "like flowing streams in a dry land",
          "and the shade of a massive rock in an arid land."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then the eyes of those who see will not be closed,",
          "and the ears of those who hear will listen."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The reckless mind will gain knowledge,",
          "and the stammering tongue will speak clearly and fluently."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A fool will no longer be called a noble,",
          "nor a scoundrel said to be important."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For a fool speaks foolishness",
          "and his mind plots iniquity.",
          "He lives in a godless way",
          "and speaks falsely about the Lord.",
          "He leaves the hungry empty",
          "and deprives the thirsty of drink."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The scoundrel’s weapons are destructive;",
          "he hatches plots to destroy the needy with lies,",
          "even when the poor person says what is right."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But a noble person plans noble things;",
          "he stands up for noble causes."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Stand up, you complacent women;",
          "listen to me.",
          "Pay attention to what I say,",
          "you overconfident daughters."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "In a little more than a year",
          "you overconfident ones will shudder,",
          "for the grapes will fail",
          "and the harvest will not come."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Shudder, you complacent ones;",
          "tremble, you overconfident ones!",
          "Strip yourselves bare",
          "and put sackcloth around your waists."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Beat your breasts in mourning",
          "for the delightful fields and the fruitful vines,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "for the ground of my people",
          "growing thorns and briers,",
          "indeed, for every joyous house in the jubilant city."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For the palace will be deserted,",
          "the busy city abandoned.",
          "The hill and the watchtower will become",
          "barren places forever,",
          "the joy of wild donkeys,",
          "and a pasture for flocks,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "until the Spirit from on high is poured out on us.",
          "Then the desert will become an orchard,",
          "and the orchard will seem like a forest."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then justice will inhabit the wilderness,",
          "and righteousness will dwell in the orchard."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The result of righteousness will be peace;",
          "the effect of righteousness",
          "will be quiet confidence forever."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then my people will dwell in a peaceful place,",
          "in safe and secure dwellings."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But hail will level the forest, ,",
          "and the city will sink into the depths."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You will be happy as you sow seed",
          "beside abundant water,",
          "and as you let oxen and donkeys range freely."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
